/target
/data

# GitKB
#
# The store is tracked deliberately: it holds the specs, ADRs and tasks, and with no sync
# remote configured an ignored store exists only on one machine — unbacked-up and invisible to
# anyone who clones. It earned this: a `repair projection` run against a stale store dropped
# the KB from 64 documents to 1, and only a previously committed snapshot made recovery
# possible.
#
# `.kb/workspaces/` is a materialized copy of the store for editing, so tracking it would
# duplicate every document. `.kb/workspace/` holds scratch checkouts. The cache is ~300MB.
.kb/.cache/
.kb/workspace/
.kb/workspaces/
.claude/plans
docs/superpowers/

